<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-247] UI assumes WebSocket connection state as disconnected</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-247</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;UI (navbar.controller.js) assumes WebSocket connection as disconnected.&lt;br/&gt;
It should get the state from WebSocketService.&lt;/p&gt;


&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;var&lt;/span&gt; vm = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;this&lt;/span&gt;;
vm.notes = notebookListDataFactory;
vm.connected = &lt;span class=&quot;code-keyword&quot;&gt;false&lt;/span&gt;
vm.websocketMsgSrv = websocketMsgSrv;
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;where as it should be something like &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;vm.connected = websocketMsgSrv.isConnected();
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</description>
